115: 
116: ## 6. Remediation plan (ordered)
117: 
118: ### Step 0 — Rotate the token now — TODO
119: Regenerate `MCP_AUTH_TOKEN` with `openssl rand -hex 32`, set in Railway only, never paste into a chat. Note: as with Basecamp, rotation is hygiene, not the fix. **Additionally**, because this server holds your Cronometer password, if you ran the PoC or otherwise suspect exposure, plan to change the Cronometer account password too (§3.5).
120: 
121: ### Step 1 — Add `MCP_APPROVE_SECRET` (required for remote) — PROPOSED
122: A secret the human types once at the `/authorize` page. Separate from `MCP_AUTH_TOKEN` (browser-form exposure vs. header-only). Minimum length 16.
123: 
124: ### Step 2 — Gate `/authorize` behind the approval secret — PROPOSED (closes §3.1)
125: Add a password field to the approve page; validate it (constant-time) on POST before issuing a code.
126: 
127: ### Step 3 — Fail closed when no auth is configured — PROPOSED (closes §3.2)
128: For `sse` / `streamable-http` transports, refuse to start unless both `MCP_AUTH_TOKEN` and `MCP_APPROVE_SECRET` are set. Remove the "unauthenticated fallback"; downgrade it to a hard error. (stdio transport, used locally, needs neither and is unaffected.)
129: 
130: ### Step 4 — Auth-code TTL — PROPOSED (closes §3.3)
131: Store `created_at`; reject codes older than 5 minutes at `/token`.
132: 
133: ### Step 5 — Constant-time comparisons — PROPOSED (closes §3.4)
134: `hmac.compare_digest` for the bearer check and the new approve-secret check.
135: 
136: ### Step 6 — Per-IP rate limiting on `/authorize` failures — PROPOSED
137: 5 failed attempts/minute/IP → 429. **Proxy-aware:** behind Railway's edge, the real client IP is in `X-Forwarded-For`, not the socket peer. (This is the lesson from the Basecamp build — `app.set("trust proxy", 1)` there.) In this ASGI server there is no Express `trust proxy`; derive the client IP by taking the **last** entry of `X-Forwarded-For` (the value appended by Railway's trusted edge), NOT the left-most (client-controlled, spoofable). If `X-Forwarded-For` is absent, fall back to the ASGI `client` peer. Document the one-hop assumption.
138: 
139: ### Step 7 — HTML-escape the authorize page — PROPOSED (closes §3.6)
140: Escape all interpolated query-param values.
141: 
142: ### Step 8 — Env hygiene — PROPOSED (addresses §3.5)
143: Confirm Railway 2FA. Consider a dedicated Cronometer account. There are no volume-seed vars to delete here (unlike Basecamp).
144: 
145: ---
146: 
147: ## 7. Proposed code changes (for reviewer to evaluate)
148: 
149: All in `server.py`. Because this is ASGI middleware rather than Express, the structure differs from Basecamp but the logic is the same.
150: 
151: ### 7a. Module-level helpers (top of file, near imports)
152: 
153: ```python
154: import hmac
155: import time
156: from hashlib import sha256
157: 
158: 
159: def _safe_equal(a: str, b: str) -> bool:
160:     """Constant-time string comparison (length-independent)."""
161:     return hmac.compare_digest(sha256(a.encode()).digest(), sha256(b.encode()).digest())
162: 
163: 
164: def _html_escape(s: str | None) -> str:
165:     s = s or ""
166:     return (
167:         s.replace("&", "&amp;")
168:         .replace("<", "&lt;")
169:         .replace(">", "&gt;")
170:         .replace('"', "&quot;")
171:     )
172: ```
173: 
174: ### 7b. Middleware constructor — accept the approve secret + add stores
175: 
176: ```python
177: def __init__(
178:     self,
179:     app,
180:     *,
181:     client_id: str,
182:     client_secret: str,
183:     access_token: str,
184:     approve_secret: str,            # NEW
185:     base_url: str = "",
186: ):
187:     self.app = app
188:     self.client_id = client_id
189:     self.client_secret = client_secret
190:     self.access_token = access_token
191:     self.approve_secret = approve_secret          # NEW
192:     self.base_url = base_url.rstrip("/")
193:     self._pending_codes: dict[str, dict] = {}
194:     # NEW: per-IP failed-attempt tracking for /authorize
195:     self._auth_attempts: dict[str, dict] = {}     # ip -> {count, reset_at}
196: 
197: CODE_TTL_S = 5 * 60
198: MAX_AUTH_ATTEMPTS = 5
199: AUTH_WINDOW_S = 60
200: ```
201: 
202: (Define the three constants at module scope or as class attributes — reviewer's preference.)
203: 
204: ### 7c. Bearer check — constant-time (in `__call__`)
205: 
206: ```python
207: auth_value = headers.get(b"authorization", b"").decode()
208: expected = f"Bearer {self.access_token}"
209: if not _safe_equal(auth_value, expected):
210:     # ... existing 401 response ...
211: ```
212: 
213: ### 7d. Client-IP helper (proxy-aware)
214: 
215: ```python
216: def _client_ip(self, scope, headers) -> str:
217:     xff = headers.get(b"x-forwarded-for", b"").decode()
218:     if xff:
219:         # Railway's edge appends the real client IP as the LAST entry.
220:         # The left-most entries are client-supplied and spoofable, so do
221:         # NOT trust them. One-hop assumption (Railway edge in front).
222:         return xff.split(",")[-1].strip()
223:     client = scope.get("client")
224:     return client[0] if client else "unknown"
225: ```
226: 
